          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              \-functor
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of the notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            to the setting of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-categories
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-categories)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"} lax functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functor"} strict 2-functor
          %p For the various separate definitions that do collapse to standard functors, see:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functor"} strict 2-functor
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo+functor"} pseudo functor
          %p
            There is also a notion of ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"}> lax functor
            ’, however this notion does not necessarily yield a standard functor when considered on discrete hom-categories.
          %p
            For the generalisation of this to higher categories, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistrict+higher+category"} semistrict higher category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Here we present explicitly the definition for the middling notion of a pseudofunctor, and comment on alterations that yield the stronger and weaker notions.
          %h4#pseudofunctor_between_strict_categories
            Pseudofunctor between strict
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℭ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{D}
            be strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℭ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\mathfrak{C}\to\mathfrak{D}
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A function
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi Ob
                          %mi ℭ
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Ob
                          %mi 𝔇
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:Ob_\mathfrak{C}\to Ob_\mathfrak{D}
            %li
              %p
                For each pair of objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
